.TH smi-greenmail "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Server Command"
.SH NAME
smi-greenmail \- Start the GreenMail standalone mail server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-greenmail
.RI [ JAVA_ARGS\| .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-greenmail
starts the GreenMail standalone mail server bound to localhost only.
No options are required; all ports, user credentials, and working directory
are configured automatically from the environment.
.PP
All standard mail protocols are enabled simultaneously:
SMTP, SMTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, POP3, POP3S, and the REST API.
Every protocol is bound exclusively to
.B 127.0.0.1
and is not reachable from outside the machine.
.PP
The mail user account is derived from the logged-in OS user:
the username matches the OS login name and the password is the login name
with
.B 123
appended.
The e-mail address is
.IB username @smtp.test\fR.
.PP
The working directory is created automatically if it does not exist.
.PP
The JAR is located via
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
so renaming the installation provider requires no changes to this script.
.PP
Any arguments supplied are passed through to the JVM unchanged.
JVM options may also be supplied via the
.SM JAVA_OPTS
environment variable.
.SH PORTS
.TP
.B 3025
SMTP
.TP
.B 3465
SMTPS
.TP
.B 3143
IMAP
.TP
.B 3993
IMAPS
.TP
.B 3110
POP3
.TP
.B 3995
POP3S
.TP
.B 8025
REST API (http://127.0.0.1:8025)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Additional JVM options (e.g.\&
.BR "\-Xmx256m" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $(smi-home-location)/greenmail
Working directory; created automatically if absent.
.TP
.I $(smi-lib-location)/greenmail-standalone.jar
GreenMail standalone JAR; installed by
.BR smi-install-package (1)
with package name
.BR greenmail .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start with all defaults:
.RS
.B smi-greenmail
.RE
.PP
Start with extra heap:
.RS
.B JAVA_OPTS="-Xmx512m" smi-greenmail
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-lib-location (1),
.BR smi-home-location (1),
.BR smi-install-package (1)
